> What you say makes sense, however I've ran out of stamina while only
> burdened, numerous times.

OK, the relevant check is (domove() in hack.c)

if(((wtcap = near_capacity()) >= OVERLOADED
	    || (wtcap > SLT_ENCUMBER &&
		(Upolyd ? (u.mh < 5 && u.mh != u.mhmax)
			: (u.uhp < 10 && u.uhp != u.uhpmax))))
	   && !Is_airlevel(&u.uz)) {
	    if(wtcap < OVERLOADED) {
		You("don't have enough stamina to move.");
		exercise(A_CON, FALSE);
	    } else
		You("collapse under your load.");
	    nomul(0);
	    return;
	}

so you are unable to move if overloaded or worse than burdened and low 
on HP (less than 10).

> Needless to say, I had no chance to survive.
> I'm pretty sure stamina is a value.
> If I rest after running out, I can
> move again after a bit.

OK, hack.c says that you lose HP when running around strained or worse, 
and you can move again when it regenerates to 10 or above.

> You're right in that if you're overloaded you can't move, but not
